@musictopia2, the `Blazor Web App` project template includes a `using static` in `_Imports.razor` to allow you to write `@rendermode InteractiveAuto`:

```razor
@using static Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web.RenderMode
```

However, the Razor Class Library template has no such `using static` directive. So, you'll either have to add that line to your RCL's `_Imports.razor` file, or declare a component's render mode by partially qualifying `InteractiveAuto`:

```razor
@rendermode RenderMode.InteractiveAuto
```

Furthermore, it looks like `BlazorWeb.Client` in your repro project doesn't reference the `BlazorShared` project. This will be required if you want components in the `BlazorShared` RCL to render using WebAssembly interactivity, as they might if they use the `InteractiveAuto` render mode.

I suspect a similar issue might be the cause of @mkalinski93's error, and possibly @bertutron's as well, although it's hard to tell without a repro project.

Found a ugly work-around:

In the Razor Class Library write a class with a static variable holding the AppType.
```
    public enum AppType { Unknown, Blazor, Maui }
    public class AppProps {
         public static AppType AppType { get; set; } = AppType.Unknown;
    }
```
Set the AppType in Program.cs `AppProps.AppType = AppType.Blazor;` and in MauiProgram.cs `AppProps.AppType = AppType.Maui;`  accordingly.

From Counter.razor remove `@page "/counter"` and `<PageTitle>Counter</PageTitle>`.

Create a CounterPage.razor component as wrapper:
```
@page "/counter"
<PageTitle>Counter</PageTitle>

@if (AppProps.AppType == AppType.Blazor) {
    <Counter @rendermode="InteractiveServer"></Counter>
} else if (AppProps.AppType == AppType.Maui) {
    <Counter></Counter>
}
```

So Counter.razor still can be used as 'page' and can be shared across the Blazor and the Maui app.

I hope I can remove this work-around soon, when there is a solution for .net 8!

Hope it may help somebody meanwhile, coming across the same issue.

The solution is somewhat complex

You do need to use the reference in your _imports.razor for the razor library
@using static Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web.RenderMode

You need to place this at the top of your page in razor library
@page "/countdown"
@rendermode RenderMode.InteractiveAuto

You then need to add the following to the program.cs file
In my case my component page is Countdown

app.MapRazorComponents<App>()
    .AddInteractiveServerRenderMode()
    .AddInteractiveWebAssemblyRenderMode()
    .AddAdditionalAssemblies(typeof(Counter).Assembly)
    .AddAdditionalAssemblies(typeof(Countdown).Assembly);
    
 You can then go to the page specified /countdown
 
 If you don't want to have it be a page, remove both of these from your component
 @page "/countdown"
@rendermode RenderMode.InteractiveAuto

Put the component on the page
<Countdown @rendermode="RenderMode.InteractiveServer"/>
